    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9258": {
      "title": "Indigenous Governance and Business Management Sessional Lecturer (Casual/Part-Time)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Indigenous Governance and Business Management Sessional Lecturer (Casual/Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Indigenous Governance and Business Management Sessional Lecturer (Casual/Part-Time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply to this position, please refer to “ Careers at the U ” on the University of Lethbridge Human Resources webpage. Applicants should include: A CV highlighting your professional qualifications, work experience, and any relevant teaching experience (courses taught, textbooks used, where and when taught) Previous teaching evaluations, if applicable Names and contact information for two references Posting Details Position Information Job Title Indigenous Governance and Business Management Sessional Lecturer (Casual/Part-Time) About the University It’s your time to shine! Work where the world comes to create, discover and learn. We are consistently one of Canada’s top-ranked universities and leading research institutions. With more than 8,900 students, two campuses (Lethbridge and Calgary), seven faculties and schools, and more than 2,500 employees, uLethbridge is Lethbridge’s second largest employer. Faculty and staff come together to contribute, each in their own way, to establishing uLethbridge as Canada’s destination university. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. The University is located in traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as Aboriginal peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. Rank Sessional Lecturer/Instructor Tenure Information Position Details The Dhillon School of Business invites applications for Sessional Lecturers in the area of Indigenous Governance & Business Management. Indigenous governance and business management ( IGBM ) provides Indigenous and non-Indigenous graduates with skills to take on leadership and managerial roles in band administration, the not-for-profit sector, Indigenous liaison work, federal and international relations, oil and gas, agriculture or your own entrepreneurial enterprises. For more information about this area of study, visit our website at www.ulethbridge.ca/future-student/program/indigenous-governance-and-business-management . Sessional Lecturers teach 1-3 courses in an academic year, as this is a casual or part-time position. Some courses may be taught online, so long as the lecturer is in Canada. The Dhillon School of Business is an AACSB Accredited School with approximately 50 full-time faculty members and roughly 1,700 students in a variety of undergraduate majors. For more information about the School, visit our website at: www.ulethbridge.ca/dhillon . Information about the University of Lethbridge can be found at https://www.ulethbridge.ca/ . We look for dedicated and inspired professionals and educators who encourage students to strive for excellence not only in the classroom but in the way they apply their knowledge to their communities and careers. All applicants are thanked in advance for their interest. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. Qualifications: Professional experience in a related field Previous teaching experience at the post-secondary level is preferred A graduate degree is desirable Indigenous knowledge and experience is required In accordance with Section 10.1 of the Alberta Human Rights Act , selection for the position will be limited to Indigenous/Aboriginal People. Candidates will be asked to self-identify as part of the application process. Position Category Faculty Dhillon School of Business Campus Lethbridge or Calgary Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants To apply to this position, please refer to “ Careers at the U ” on the University of Lethbridge Human Resources webpage. Applicants should include: A CV highlighting your professional qualifications, work experience, and any relevant teaching experience (courses taught, textbooks used, where and when taught) Previous teaching evaluations, if applicable Names and contact information for two references Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letters of Recommendation Optional Documents Additional Documents Letters of Recommendation #2 Letters of Recommendation #3 Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). In accordance with Section 10.1 of the Alberta Human Rights Act, selection for the position will be limited to Indigenous/Aboriginal People. Your answer to this question will be held in confidence by Human Resources, and only shared confidentially with the search committee.  Do you identify as an Indigenous/Aboriginal Person? Yes No I prefer not to respond at this time The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/8841": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant (Research)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant (Research) - Full Fixed About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Not Applicable Position Details We’re Hiring: Graduate Instructional Assistant – Graduate Peer Mentor Program & Orientation Want to create learning experiences that shape the next generation of graduate leaders? The School of Graduate Studies is looking for a Graduate Instructional Assistant to design interactive, engaging training for our Graduate Peer Mentor Program and review our orientation modules for the School of Graduate Studies. What you’ll do: Build and review online modules in Moodle and Arise. Turn a three-term mentorship curriculum into interactive, reflective, and scenario-based learning. Collaborate with graduate staff, mentors, and experts to ensure content is accurate, inclusive, and aligned with holistic development principles. Ensure our Graduate Studies Orientation ( GSO ) Modules are up-to-date. What we’re looking for: Experience in instructional design, e-learning, and adult learning. Skilled with Moodle and simulation-based learning (Arise preferred). Creative, collaborative, and passionate about graduate student success. Apply now – help us empower new graduate students at the beginning of their studies and mentors to guide peers academically, professionally, and personally! Please note: Only registered University of Lethbridge graduate students are eligible to apply for this posting. Graduate Assistant wages will be paid according to Schedule A of the ULGSA Collective Agreement. Position Category Graduate Assistant Faculty Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 12/10/2025 Close Date 01/04/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/19/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 04/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/8910": {
      "title": "Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Health Sciences - Nursing Sessional Instructor About the University It’s your time to shine! Work where the world comes to create, discover and learn. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions. With more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students, two campuses (Lethbridge and Calgary), seven faculties and schools, and more than 2,500 employees, ULethbridge is Lethbridge’s second largest employer. Faculty and staff come together to contribute, each in their own way, to establishing ULethbridge as Canada’s destination university. In 2022, Lethbridge was recognized as one of Canada’s top small cities. Rank Tenure Information Position Details If you are open to innovation and committed to the creation of an environment that excites and ignites learning, we welcome your application. The Faculty of Health Sciences is an open, fair, honest, caring and collaborative community that strives to provide a rich education grounded in real world practice, drawing from the knowledge and expertise of multiple health disciplines. Position The Faculty of Health Sciences at the University of Lethbridge invites applications for sessional (part-time) instructors to teach 6 and/or 12 week clinical courses in the Fall, Spring and Summer semesters . Qualifications The successful candidates must be regulated members, in good standing, with the College of Registered Nurses of Alberta ( CRNA ). The candidates will also have at least five years of nursing practice in acute medical, and surgical settings. Applicants must have a Baccalaureate degree in nursing. The ideal candidate will also possess excellent communication, mentorship, and organizational skills, and maintain excellent working relationships with all nursing faculty, students, members of the University community and our service delivery partners. Candidates must demonstrate leadership in professional nursing practice in interdisciplinary settings . A thorough and current knowledge of nursing skills, procedures, and equipment related to nursing practice settings is required. Previous teaching experience is preferred. Academic Setting The CASN accredited four-year BN and 23-month BN After-Degree programs are offered in collaboration with Lethbridge College within the Nursing Education in Southwestern Alberta ( NESA ) Programs. Students practice in rural and urban settings including institutional and community locations. The University of Lethbridge has a reputation for providing a high-quality education and has been rated #1 for research activities among institutions of our size in Canada. The university website contains more information about our institution. To view additional information about the Faculty of Health Sciences, please visit our website at www.uleth.ca/hlsc . Remuneration You will receive an excellent salary commensurate with your experience, an annual professional development allowance, as well as a benefit package, including a tuition benefit for University of Lethbridge programming, and relocation assistance. Please visit The University of Lethbridge website to view the economic benefits package outlined in the Academic Staff Collective Agreement, https://www.ulethbridge.ca/hr/university-lethbridge-faculty-association-ulfa-faculty-handbook . Employment Equity In accordance with Canadian Immigration Regulation, first preference will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents of Canada. The University is an inclusive and equitable campus encouraging applications from qualified women and men including persons with disabilities, members of visible minorities, and Aboriginal persons. All positions are subject to Board approval. How to Apply All applications must be submitted online and must include a cover letter, contact information for three academic references who will be asked to provide reference letters, a detailed curriculum-vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Referees will be contacted directly, with information on how to submit their reference letters; the application submission will automatically trigger this request to your references. For enquiries about this position, please contact Pam Smith, Administrative Manager, Faculty of Health Sciences, at pamela.smith4@uleth.ca Position Category Faculty Faculty of Health Sciences Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/28/2023 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9206": {
      "title": "Liberal Education Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Liberal Education Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Liberal Education Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Liberal Education Assistant Professor About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. The University of Lethbridge is a comprehensive and research-intensive university founded on the principles of liberal education where inspired scholars integrate research and creative activity with teaching. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. Founded in 1967 on traditional Blackfoot land, it is a place where student engagement in learning, creative activities, and research takes place every day. With campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary, the University of Lethbridge offers more than 150 undergraduate and 60 graduate programs in the Faculties of Arts & Science, Education, Fine Arts, Health Sciences, the Schools of Liberal Education and Graduate Studies, and the Dhillon School of Business, to more than 8,000 students. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Position Details Position Description The School of Liberal Education at the University of Lethbridge invites applications for a tenure-track position in Liberal Education at the rank of Assistant Professor with a start date of January 1, 2027, subject to budgetary approval. A start date of July 1, 2027 is also possible. Hiring salary will be in the range of $86,470 to $98,000 per year, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will be expected to undertake interdisciplinary teaching and research in the School of Liberal Education. The successful candidate will develop and teach courses addressing a broad range of quantitative or science-related topics and principles to a wide variety of undergraduate students with different majors. The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. (or a nearly completed Ph.D. with a defence date scheduled) and have a strong quantitative background. A graduate degree in a STEM discipline or in Health Sciences would be an asset. A clear demonstration of teaching proficiency as the primary instructor in one or more undergraduate courses is essential. The School is particularly interested in applicants with a background or interest in Indigenous Science, land-based learning, climate science, or environmental science. Required Documents An application should include: A letter of application expressing interest in the position that articulates i) the candidate’s understanding of liberal education and how it relates to their potential contributions to this position; and ii) the candidate’s commitment to collegiality. A curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy and approach (not exceeding two pages) A statement of research interests (not exceeding two pages) Contact information for two referees who can speak to the candidate’s achievement in or potential to contribute to teaching and research in the School of Liberal Education The Committee will begin reviewing applications on September 15, 2026. For inquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Harold Jansen, Dean, School of Liberal Education at libadmin@uleth.ca. While all applications will be considered, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. Understanding that career interruptions can have an impact on a candidate’s record of achievement, we encourage applicants to explain in their applications any impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The School of Liberal Education Founded in 2017, the School of Liberal Education is a small unit of faculty members and instructors at the University of Lethbridge who are distinguished by their commitment to interdisciplinary teaching and research. The School’s academic staff teach a variety of undergraduate courses in liberal education to a diverse student body. Faculty members are expected to develop and maintain research programs. There are opportunities to collaborate with other faculty members across the University. The City of Lethbridge The city of Lethbridge has over 100,000 people and is located in Southern Alberta, not far from the Rocky Mountains and the U.S. border. Lethbridge enjoys a sunny, dry climate that is surprisingly mild, has excellent cultural and recreational amenities, and offers attractive economic conditions including affordable housing. For more information see the City’s website at www.lethbridge.ca. Position Category Research Faculty Faculty of Education Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interest Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). I authorize the University of Lethbridge to disclose the personal information submitted as my application package to the search committee and members of the department for the purpose of administering the selection process for this position. This consent is valid for the period of one year from the date the application information is submitted. I agree I dont agree The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9229": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | SharePoint Analyst (Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help SharePoint Analyst (Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title SharePoint Analyst (Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The University of Lethbridge is seeking a SharePoint Analyst to assist with the planning and implementation of campus-wide electronic records management initiatives using Microsoft SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview. This is a two-year (2) term position located at our Lethbridge campus. Position Overview: As the SharePoint Analyst, you will play a central role in advancing the university’s use of SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview for records and information management. Working with a small team of technical specialists and process owners, you will help translate business and records management needs into practical configuration, administration, and support activities within SharePoint Online. The position will also support the planned use of Microsoft Purview capabilities, including sensitivity labels, retention policies, and retention labels across administrative and research areas. This position reports to the Director of Infrastructure and works closely with the Records and Information Manager, Security and Systems teams, as well as academic and administrative units. Key Responsibilities: Understand Business Requirements Work to understand the needs of the business and match them with capabilities of the Purview and SharePoint Online applications to optimize the management of electronic documents. Implement Electronic Records Management Serve as the technical expert for SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview to assist in developing an effective electronic document records management program with a small team. Leverage and Grow the Usage of Tools Assist users to leverage tools such as SharePoint Online and Microsoft Purview to manage the lifecycle of digital records. Configure SharePoint Online for efficient and appropriate record storage. Create and administer sensitivity labels, retention policies and labels to manage data. This will help teams to protect sensitive information and ensure the university meets its legal and regulatory obligations. Configure SharePoint Online Assist business users in configuring document repositories within SharePoint sites to conform electronic records management program once developed. The University of Lethbridge is undertaking a job classification and compensation review for Administrative Professional Officer ( APO ) positions. As such, the salary range currently assigned for this position may be adjusted as a result of this project. Position Qualifications Education: University degree in a relevant field (e.g. data science, computer science, etc). Experience: Experience administering and configuring a Microsoft SharePoint Online tenant is required. Experience with Microsoft Purview would be ideal. Experience in a post-secondary environment is preferred. Skills: 2+ years of experience configuring and managing a SharePoint Online tenant as an administrator Experience working with records management and electronic document management system implementations Familiarity with Microsoft Purview or other Microsoft 365 compliance features would be considered an asset Excellent planning, coordination, and interpersonal skills Strong written and verbal communication Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $66,716.84 - $83,930.19 annually Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $66,716.84 - $101,143.54 annually (APO - Grade 3) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group APO Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 09/01/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9329": {
      "title": "Faculty of Education - Counselling Psychology Sessional Lecturer",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Education - Counselling Psychology Sessional Lecturer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Education - Counselling Psychology Sessional Lecturer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A cover letter, full curriculum vitae, and the names of three references should be addressed to Dr. Lisa Starr, Dean, Faculty of Education, University of Lethbridge, 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta, T1K 3M4. The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Education - Counselling Psychology Sessional Lecturer About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Sessional Lecturer/Instructor Tenure Information Term Position Details The Faculty of Education at the University of Lethbridge is seeking a Sessional Lecturer to teach courses within the Master of Counselling and MEd Counselling Psychology programs in the Winter 2027 term. Specific courses include: CAAP 6617 Research and Program Evaluation Skills – This course is offered asynchronously. Candidates should possess significant experience with teaching research and program evaluation classes and/or conducting similar research. EDUC 5621 Counselling Psychology: Ethics and Professional Practice – This course is offered on campus in Lethbridge once per week. Candidates should possess significant experience with teaching ethics and/or have significant professional exposure to ethics. Candidates for this class must be Registered Psychologists in Alberta. EDUC 5706 Counselling Psychology: Interventions – This course is offered on campus in Lethbridge once per week. Candidates should possess significant experience with teaching interventions and/or have significant professional experience in delivering evidence-based interventions. Candidates for this class must be Registered Psychologists in Alberta. Applicants with a graduate degree in psychology or related discipline are invited to apply. Previous experience teaching at the graduate level is an asset. Individuals contracted as a Sessional Lecturer will be asked to become an Associate Member of the School of Graduate Studies. Individuals seeking Sessional Lecturer positions teaching within the B.Ed. program should apply separately to the undergraduate program. Position Category Faculty Faculty of Education Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants A cover letter, full curriculum vitae, and the names of three references should be addressed to Dr. Lisa Starr, Dean, Faculty of Education, University of Lethbridge, 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta, T1K 3M4. The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae References Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9320": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant (Non-Teaching)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant (Non-Teaching) – Communications, Web &amp; Events (Full Fixed) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Non-Teaching) – Communications, Web & Events (Full Fixed) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant (Non-Teaching) – Communications, Web & Events (Full Fixed) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Not Applicable Position Details Position Description: i4Geo is seeking a Graduate Assistant (Non-Teaching) to support the Institute’s communications, web presence, outreach, and events. Responsibilities: Assist with website updates, content creation, and general web maintenance. Create and manage content for i4Geo social media channels. Assist with planning, promoting, and coordinating workshops, seminars, and other events. Develop promotional materials, presentations, and event communications. Assist with event registration, logistics, photography, and post-event communications. Support other i4Geo communications, outreach, and related activities as needed. Qualifications: Current University of Lethbridge graduate student. Strong written communication and organizational skills. Experience with social media and digital content creation. Experience or familiarity with website editing and content management. Proficiency with Microsoft Office; experience with Canva, Adobe, or similar design tools is an asset. Ability to work independently, manage multiple tasks, and meet deadlines. Interest or experience in GIS , remote sensing, geography, or related fields is an asset. Please note: Only registered University of Lethbridge graduate students are eligible to apply for this posting. Graduate Assistant wages will be paid according to Schedule A of the ULGSA Collective Agreement. Position Category Graduate Assistant Faculty Faculty of Arts & Science Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/09/2026 Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9328": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Electrician (Full-time, Continuing) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Electrician (Full-time, Continuing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Electrician (Full-time, Continuing) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The University of Lethbridge is seeking a full-time, continuing position as an Electrician. This position maintains a safe, stable, and comfortable learning, living and working environment on campus. To accomplish this, requires the operation and maintenance of the entire electrical system on campus, including emergency and life safety systems. This position requires a high degree of self-reliance, team coordination, extensive knowledge base in practical electrical applications, theory, and code. Extensive knowledge of on-campus and off-campus buildings and the need to be comfortable in making autonomous technical decisions while on standby, that can potentially impact the campus electrical system, research, and life safety on a significant level under stressful or a time constrained period. The electrical team is comprised of 5 electricians who form a rotation for regular and standby (after-hours) duties ensuring a response to issues all hours of the day. Position Qualifications Minimum grade 12 education and an Alberta Journeyman Electrical Certificate or out of province Red Seal designation. Along with the educational background, applicants should have 6 years relevant experience in an industrial and institutional maintenance setting. This experience can be through a combination of apprenticeship and journeyman positions. Master Electrician certification and greater number of year’s experience are considered assets. Ability to demonstrate their experience with variable frequency drives, co-generation systems, 15KV power distribution systems, medium voltage switching, SCADA system, lighting control systems, security access systems, low-voltage controls, UPS systems, and a strong knowledge of the Canadian Electrical Code. Experience with line locates and thermography are considered assets. Possess certificates in the following: WHMIS , Personal Fall Protection, Mobile Elevating Work Platform, Arc Flash and High Voltage Safety. A valid unrestricted Class 5 Driver’s License with no more than 6 demerits and submission of a motor vehicle record (driver abstract) dated within 3 months of the posting close is required. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,782.00 - $6,545.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,782.00 - $7,308.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 12) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/12/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9346": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Project Manager (Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Project Manager (Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Project Manager (Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Project Management Office – Facilities at the University of Lethbridge is currently inviting applications for a 3-year term position as a Project Manager to start as soon as possible. Reporting to the Associate Executive Director, Project Management Office, the successful candidate will be responsible for providing design services and project management expertise for all phases of maintenance, renovation and construction projects. The successful candidate must be able to administer professional services agreements, develop project budgets, develop contracting strategies, determine user requirements and ensure the accurate reflection of those requirements in construction documents. Other duties include the preparation of tender documents, contracts, contract administration, developing cost estimates, performing on site construction observations and managing the implementation of approved projects within a project management system. The University of Lethbridge is undertaking a job classification and compensation review for Administrative Professional Officer ( APO ) positions. As such, the salary range currently assigned for this position may be adjusted as a result of this project. Position Qualifications The ideal candidate will have a University Degree and a minimum of 3 years of experience, or a College Diploma and a minimum of 5 years of experience, all of which should relate to the construction project management or construction experience. Equivalent combinations of education and construction experience will be considered. Project Management qualifications, professional designations relevant to the construction industry, and experience in developing cost estimates for building systems in an institutional or commercial environment would be considered an asset. The position requires excellent communication and organizational skills with the ability to exercise independent judgment and manage projects on time and on budget. The successful candidate will be required to provide a satisfactory Criminal Record Check. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $77,111.09 - $97,005.51 annually Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $77,111.09 - $116,899.94 annually (APO - Grade 4) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group APO Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/26/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 03/30/2029 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9349": {
      "title": "Faculty of Fine Arts - Sessional Lecturer",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Fine Arts - Sessional Lecturer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Fine Arts - Sessional Lecturer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit your application to Dean of Fine Arts, Dr. Heather Davis-Fisch, by email to Sarah Hilliard at finearts.dean@uleth.ca , and include in the subject line “Application for Sessional Instruction”. Applications should include a curriculum vitae, previous teaching evaluations (if applicable), up to three (3) letters of reference, and a letter of application, indicating the desired area of instruction within the Faculty of Fine Arts. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Fine Arts - Sessional Lecturer About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 7,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Lecturer Tenure Information Non-Tenure Track Position Details The Faculty of Fine Arts at the University of Lethbridge invites applications for prospective Sessional Lecturer employment opportunities. The Faculty offers courses in Art, Art History, Museum Studies, Drama, Music, Digital Audio Arts, New Media, and Cinema. We are seeking applications in all areas, at the 1000, 2000, and 3000-level of instruction, and will follow up with applicants directly in the event that an opportunity does become available. The closing date for applications is September 15, 2026, though late applications may also be considered. Additionally, we are seeking up to two candidates to teach the following Winter 2027 courses: Art NOW Built upon a series of guest lectures by nationally and internationally recognized artists and art professionals, this course covers a wide range of current topics in contemporary art. Guest lecture presentations are supplemented by contextual lectures, readings, visits to local art exhibitions and discussion. The candidate must: have a demonstrated ability to contextualize contemporary art for a wide audience have a demonstrated ability to work flexibly and in collaboration with colleagues. be able to work with the Department’s visiting speaker committee and with local galleries and visiting artists be able to provide a welcoming introduction for speakers to the University be able to engage a wide range of students in local art experiences MFA in Art, or PhD ( ABD considered) in Art History, Museum Studies, or related field and demonstrated expertise in contemporary Canadian art; or MA in related field and equivalent curatorial experience in contemporary art Architecture and Design NOW Aspects of recent and contemporary architecture and design are introduced through a series of presentations by practicing architects, designers, architectural historians, critics and writers on design. The candidate must: have a demonstrated ability to contextualize contemporary architecture and design for a wide audience have a demonstrated ability to work flexibly and in collaboration with colleagues. be able to work with the Department’s visiting speaker committee and with local galleries and visiting artists be able to provide a welcoming introduction for speakers to the University be able to engage a wide range of students in local architecture MFA in Art, or PhD ( ABD considered) in Architectural or design history, Art History, Museum Studies, or related field and demonstrated expertise in contemporary Canadian art; or MA in related field and equivalent curatorial experience in relevant areas Applications to teach Art NOW and/or Architecture and Design NOW for the Winter 2027 semester are due no later than October 19, 2026. Please submit your application to Dean of Fine Arts, Dr. Heather Davis-Fisch, by email to Sarah Hilliard at finearts.dean@uleth.ca , and include in the subject line “Application for Sessional Instruction”. Applications should include a curriculum vitae, previous teaching evaluations (if applicable), up to three (3) letters of reference, and a letter of application, indicating the desired area of instruction within the Faculty of Fine Arts. All applicants are thanked in advance for their interest. Only those selected for interviews will be contacted. At the University of Lethbridge, fostering a culture of inclusion is an institutional imperative. The University invites and encourages applications from all qualified individuals, including from groups that are traditionally underrepresented in employment, who may contribute to further diversification of our Institution. In accordance with Canadian Immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. The University is located in traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Aboriginal peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. The Faculty of Fine Arts was gifted the Blackfoot name Piiksinaasin, Manifesting Beauty, by Dr. Leroy Little Bear, with the assistance of Elder Francis First Charger, in March 2024. Piiksinaasin, which means Manifesting Beauty, represents the Faculty of Fine Arts as a place where students create, explore and research, transforming the world around them through creative practice and critical thinking. The name reflects the Faculty’s long-standing support of Indigenous arts and creative initiatives and exemplifies the work done to advance reconciliation and decolonization. Position Category Other Faculty Faculty of Fine Arts Campus Lethbridge or Calgary Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/24/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit your application to Dean of Fine Arts, Dr. Heather Davis-Fisch, by email to Sarah Hilliard at finearts.dean@uleth.ca , and include in the subject line “Application for Sessional Instruction”. Applications should include a curriculum vitae, previous teaching evaluations (if applicable), up to three (3) letters of reference, and a letter of application, indicating the desired area of instruction within the Faculty of Fine Arts. Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae References Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Interests Optional Documents Additional Documents Teaching Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9353": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Grounds Worker II (Casual) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Grounds Worker II (Casual) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Grounds Worker II (Casual) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Department of Grounds Maintenance requires the services of a casual (20-35hours a week) Grounds Worker II to commence work as soon as possible. The successful candidate will be required to perform manual work in Grounds Maintenance and will operate various types of light and heavy duty equipment proficiently. The ability to perform strenuous physical labour under a variety of seasonal conditions is required. Safety is of paramount importance for the public, the individual, and their co-workers while producing a good volume of work. The nature of the work will vary according to seasonal changes and will include: General Grounds Maintenance such as Turf Maintenance, Bed Maintenance, Indoor Plant Maintenance, and coaching of casual summer staff Snow and Ice Removal Tree and Shrub Pruning General Cleaning of Campus Campus Improvement Projects This position will be required to work a standard work week of Monday to Friday with typical hours of 07:00 – 15:00, with the possibility of a shifting work week. Hours of may shift due to weather conditions and may be required to start work as early as 05:00. Overtime may be part of the routine as needed. Salary: $24.43 per hour Position Qualifications The successful candidate will have a High School Diploma. Preference will be given to a person with a minimum 12 months of prior related work experience and a horticultural certificate or diploma or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Certifications in mobile aerial lift use, fall protection and Standard First Aid with CPR C and AED are desired. Basic knowledge of outdoor maintenance procedures, proficiency with hand tools (powered and non-powered), proficiency with operating utility vehicles and heavy equipment, attention to surrounding environment, utilizing equipment in difficult working conditions and heavy vehicle/pedestrian traffic, basic knowledge of horticultural processes and techniques, ability to lift a minimum of 50 pounds. A valid unrestricted Class 5 Driver’s License with no more than 6 demerits and submission of a motor vehicle record (driver abstract) dated within 3 months of the posting close is also required. The successful candidate will have strong public relations skills and have knowledge of safe work practices and procedures in the grounds maintenance field. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Hiring Range indicated in Position Details Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 10/05/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9361": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Research Facilitator: Internal Awards, Postdoctoral Funding, and Research Management System Support (Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Research Facilitator: Internal Awards, Postdoctoral Funding, and Research Management System Support (Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Research Facilitator: Internal Awards, Postdoctoral Funding, and Research Management System Support (Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Office of Research and Innovation Services ( ORIS ) at the University of Lethbridge invites applications for the position of Research Facilitator: Internal Awards, Postdoctoral Funding, and Research Management System Support, starting no later than January 4, 2027. ORIS is a central support to the research community at the University of Lethbridge, and this Research Facilitator position plays a pivotal role in supporting and enhancing research and scholarly activities. As a member of a dynamic team of five research facilitators, reporting to the Director of Research and Innovation Services, the successful candidate supports research growth through grant and award administration, external funding, Research Management System ( RMS ) enhancement, and knowledge mobilization activities, including resource development. Duties and Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assist faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and undergraduate students in developing and strengthening grant proposals; Manage and coordinate internal research grants, undergraduate awards, and postdoctoral funding competitions; Advise faculty members, postdoctoral fellows, and undergraduate students on relevant university and external sponsor policies, procedures, and guidelines; Administer pre- and post-award processes, including opening research accounts, tracking renewal timelines, and ensuring reports are submitted to funders; Contribute to strategies for improving funding success rates and increasing research-related revenue; Support knowledge mobilization by helping researchers translate research into practical applications and communicate research activities and successes to the broader community; Undertake related duties, as assigned, consistent with the nature of the position. The University of Lethbridge is undertaking a job classification and compensation review for Administrative Professional Officer ( APO ) positions. As such, the salary range currently assigned for this position may be adjusted as a result of this project. Position Qualifications The ideal candidate will have a master’s degree in any discipline (a doctoral degree is an asset) and three years of experience writing and reviewing grant applications and contracts. Furthermore, the ideal candidate will have: Familiarity with Canada’s national granting councils and other major sponsors of university research; Knowledge of the university’s internal grants, undergraduate awards, postdoctoral funding; Knowledge of research administration processes and electronic research administration systems, with the ability to develop expert functional knowledge of assigned RMS (InfoEd modules); Experience configuring workflows, with strong analytical and troubleshooting skills and the ability to triage, document, reproduce, and escalate system issues; Excellent organizational and time-management skills, including experience coordinating a high volume of diverse activities, meeting tight deadlines, managing governance processes, and adapting to changing priorities; Strong technical literacy and advanced proficiency with common Microsoft Office applications, Adobe products, and business process management tools; A respectful, tactful, and diplomatic approach, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively; Effective communication, presentation, and strong interpersonal skills; A commitment to ongoing professional development and other learning opportunities; Membership in the Canadian Association of Research Administrators ( CARA ) and certification in research administration are assets. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $66,716.84 - $83,930.19 annually Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $66,716.84 - $101,143.54 annually (APO - Grade 3) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group APO Position Category Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/29/2026 Close Date 10/20/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) 02/01/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9367": {
      "title": "Faculty of Health Sciences - Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor (Anatomy/Physiology)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Health Sciences - Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor (Anatomy/Physiology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Health Sciences - Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor (Anatomy/Physiology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Health Sciences - Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor (Anatomy/Physiology) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 7,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Associate Teaching Professor Tenure Information Term Position Details Our university The University of Lethbridge ( uLethbridge ) is a comprehensive and research-intensive university founded on the principles of liberal education where inspired scholars integrate research and creative activity with teaching. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. Founded in 1967 on traditional Blackfoot land, it is a place where student engagement in learning, creative activities, and research takes place every day. With campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary, uLethbridge offers more than 150 undergraduate and 60 graduate programs in the Faculties of Arts & Science, Education, Fine Arts, Health Sciences, the Schools of Liberal Education and Graduate Studies, and the Dhillon School of Business, to more than 7,000 students. Our values Accessibility, Belonging and Community for All are key strategic priorities for the University of Lethbridge. The University of Lethbridge recognizes that diversity enriches our campus and community and is fundamental to teaching, learning, and research excellence. The university as a whole embraces equity as a core value to build strong and vibrant communities of belonging where students, faculty and staff feel welcome, are treated equitably, and can thrive. Position The Southern Alberta Medical Program and Faculty of Health Sciences invite applications for a continuing Instructor position to begin January 1, 2027, subject to budgetary approval. This is a full-time (1.0 FTE ) teaching position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor. Qualifications The successful applicant will have doctoral training in anatomy or a closely related field. Preferred qualifications include a PhD, MD, or MD/PhD, although a combination of qualifications and experience will be considered. The candidate will have experience teaching anatomy to medical students, as evidenced by a record of high-quality lecture, small group, and laboratory-based instruction. Selection criteria include academic qualifications, teaching experience, evidence of teaching quality, evidence of scholarly engagement with medical education, and educational leadership experience. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility in teaching and learning, including the use of inclusive pedagogical practices and a demonstrated decolonizing approach to medical education. The rank of the successful candidate will be determined based on their qualifications and experience. Job Duties We seek applicants with competence across a broad range of duties including, but not limited to traditional lectures, lecture video and podcast preparation, laboratory-based instruction using cadaveric specimens, small group instruction, exam setup and supervision, and remediation. This position will be located in person at the University of Lethbridge, which is situated on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. Academic Setting The position will support several programs at the University of Lethbridge, including, but not limited to, the Southern Alberta Medical Program, Nursing, Therapeutic Recreation, and Kinesiology. The successful candidate will contribute to anatomy education across these interdisciplinary programs and work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and learners across the institution. The University of Lethbridge has a reputation for providing a high-quality, approachable education and has been ranked highly for research activities among institutions of our size in Canada. The university website, www.uleth.ca, contains more information about our institution. For more information about the Faculty of Health Sciences please visit our website at: www.uleth.ca/healthsciences . Remuneration Hiring salary will be determined by the University of Lethbridge Academic Staff Collective Agreement and commensurate with qualifications and experience. In accordance with Schedule A of the 2024-2028 Academic Staff Collective Agreement, the minimum salary for an Assistant Teaching Professor is $73,159 and the minimum salary for an Associate Teaching Professor is $78,786. It is expected that the successful candidate’s salary offer will be between the minimum (as appropriate for the rank of their appointment) and $105,000. University of Lethbridge offers a comprehensive benefits package and relocation assistance. Please visit The University of Lethbridge website to view the economic benefits package outlined in the Academic Staff Collective Agreement. This position is a term University of Lethbridge Faculty Association ( ULFA ) position and is governed by the terms and conditions of the applicable collective agreement. Employment Equity In accordance with Canadian Immigration Regulation, first preference will be given to Canadian citizens and permanent residents of Canada. The University is an inclusive and equitable campus encouraging applications from qualified people of all genders, including persons with disabilities, racialized persons, and Indigenous persons. All positions are subject to Board approval. How to Apply All applications must be submitted online and must include a cover letter, contact information for three academic references who will be asked to provide reference letters, a detailed curriculum-vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and evidence of research and teaching effectiveness. Referees will be contacted directly, with information on how to submit their reference letters. The application submission will automatically trigger this request to your references. The deadline for applications is October 31, 2026. For enquiries about this position, please contact Pam Smith, Administrative Manager, Faculty of Health Sciences, at pamela.smith4@uleth.ca Position Category Faculty Faculty of Health Sciences Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 09/23/2026 Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/31/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Teaching/Research Interests Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9369": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant (Research)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Graduate Assistant (Research) – Education (Casual) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Assistant (Research) – Education (Casual) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Assistant (Research) – Education (Casual) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Tenure Information Not Applicable Position Details We are seeking a Graduate Assistant for a research project examining how teachers and principals collaborate to support students with profound and multiple disabilities. The project uses interviews and professional development workshops to develop case studies and communities of practice. Typical tasks: Conduct interviews with parents, teachers, and principals. Transcribe recordings, check transcripts for accuracy, and remove identifying information. Analyze interviews and workshop discussions using reflexive thematic analysis. Contribute to writing case studies, research reports, and manuscripts. Maintain confidentiality, organize research materials, and participate in research team meetings. Qualifications: Current enrolment in a graduate program. Interest in education, disability, and qualitative research. Strong communication, writing, and organizational skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Training and supervision will be provided; previous interviewing or qualitative analysis experience is not required. Work hours are flexible. Work may be completed on or off campus, with interview scheduling coordinated with participants. Please note: Only registered University of Lethbridge graduate students are eligible to apply for this posting. Graduate Assistant wages will be paid according to Schedule A of the ULGSA Collective Agreement. Position Category Graduate Assistant Faculty Faculty of Education Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date 10/21/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 10/26/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9341": {
      "title": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Standardized Patient, Southern Alberta Medical Program (Casual) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Standardized Patient, Southern Alberta Medical Program (Casual) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Standardized Patient, Southern Alberta Medical Program (Casual) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details Are you interested in participating in training future physicians? This is a casual role with opportunities to participate on Tuesday afternoons throughout the year and occasional exam blocks. This role may involve role play for communications, being a human subject for non invasive physical exam procedures and providing feedback to students and faculty where appropriate. Ability to provide sensitive, critical intuitive verbal and written feedback following the established model when required and adhere to strict guidelines of standardization are essential. Summary of Key Responsibilities (job functions include but are not limited to): Mental and physical stamina to reproduce exacting scenarios up to 8 or more times a day for some of the exams or courses. Able to provide sensitive, critical intuitive verbal and written feedback to faculty when required as this is utilized in the evaluation of student performance. Adhere to strict guidelines of standardization, from the first encounter to the last and with other SPs of the same case; to maintain consistency and fairness for examinations. Maintain confidentiality of information related to student performance and feedback evaluations. Apply developed knowledge and expertise successfully to roles & responsibilities and acts as a key resource to others. Role play for communications. Provide feedback to students and faculty, where appropriate. Human subject for non-evasive physical exam procedures. May be required to role play in large class setting to facilitate lectures. Starting Hourly Wage Range: $26.18 – $28.97 Full Hourly Wage Range: $26.18 – $31.74 Position Qualifications Experience in acting with post-secondary education in this field. Ability to use improvisational skills, as cases require non-text experience. Ability to memorize large amounts of complex information related to personality traits, behavioral symptoms and disease entities. Ability to accurately, convincingly and consistently interpret and present symptoms and/or information, as cued by students in a simulated situation. Ability, when requested, to provide consistent, objective and focused feedback and evaluation to students in a simulated and/or testing environment within the established feedback model. Required to maintain confidentiality of records and information. Two to four years’ experience in related position preferred. Must be able to negotiate personal boundaries and request assistance if needed. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 05/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 07/13/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/31/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9386": {
      "title": "Director, School of Engineering",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Director, School of Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director, School of Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | This posting does not accept online applications. Please contact your Human Resource Office for instructions on how to apply. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director, School of Engineering About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Associate Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Position Details The University of Lethbridge (ULethbridge) is seeking a visionary leader for the inaugural Director to establish its School of Engineering within the Faculty of Arts and Science. Building on more than 40 years of delivering a first-year engineering transfer program in collaboration with the University of Alberta, ULethbridge is launching its first four-year Bachelor of Engineering degree in Integrated Engineering and is excited to accept the first intake of students in the Fall Semester of 2027. Reporting to the Dean, Faculty of Arts and Science, the Director will lead the development of a distinctive School with its own School Council and help shape the future of engineering education in southern Alberta. The Director will oversee the strategic development of the School, from recruiting and supporting academic and technical staff, guiding curriculum and program development, to building internal and community partnerships, navigating successful national accreditation, and initiating research and graduate programming. Working collaboratively across the University, the Director will foster strong School governance, high-quality teaching and research, and the foundations for future graduate programming. This is a leadership opportunity for an academic innovator, relationship-builder, fundraiser, and strategic planner to shape the future of engineering education in southern Alberta. An active advocate and ambassador for the School, the Director will build relationships with industry, government, Indigenous communities, alumni, donors, and research partners. They will advance foundational and applied research, attract external support, and help develop the facilities and partnerships needed for the School to thrive. The Director will establish an Industry Advisory Council and expand opportunities for cooperative education, internships, capstone projects, and other forms of work-integrated learning. The Director will place students at the centre of the School’s development, creating an inclusive environment that welcomes diverse perspectives and connects engineering learning with real-world challenges. They will lead with respect and integrity, support collegial decision-making, and advance the University’s commitments to Indigenous engagement, sustainability, liberal education, accessibility, belonging, and community. The successful candidate will hold a PhD in engineering and qualify for a tenured appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. They will be required to register as a professional engineer (P.Eng.) with the Association of Professional Engineers and Geoscientists of Alberta ( APEGA ). Applicants must have at least 10 years of experience teaching, conducting research, contributing to national accreditation requirements, and providing service in and to a four-year Canadian engineering degree program. A recognized scholar with academic leadership experience, the ideal candidate will bring the vision and practical judgment to build a new School, a record of securing external funding and developing partnerships, and an inclusive, collaborative approach to leading people through change. The appointment as Director, School of Engineering is for a five-year period with the possibility of renewal. How to Apply Janet Soles and Associates has been retained to conduct this search on behalf of the University of Lethbridge. For more information about this opportunity or to apply , please send an email in confidence to apply@jssearch.ca with the subject line “Director, School of Engineering”. Applications should include a curriculum vitae and letter of interest. About The University of Lethbridge The University of Lethbridge is Iniskim, or Sacred Buffalo Stone, and is located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta. Thanks to a determined and forward-thinking group of citizens who believed southern Alberta warranted its own university, ULethbridge opened its doors in 1967 and established our home in west Lethbridge. In 1996, the University opened its Calgary Campus. ULethbridge has supported the region, Alberta, and Canada through teaching, research, and outreach activities, and has prepared tens of thousands of graduates to make important contributions in communities around the world. Each year, ULethbridge welcomes approximately 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students from nearly 100 countries to our campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. Today, approximately 55,000 ULethbridge alumni are making important contributions in communities across the globe. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds, ensuring all students find their place and purpose here. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for both our students and employees. Leveraging the depth of student engagement enabled by our smaller size, we distinguish ourselves by holding the undergraduate and graduate student experience at the forefront of our exceptional teaching, research, and support activities. Our liberal education approach enables students and alumni to critically integrate ideas and experiences across disciplines, equipping them with the adaptive thinking and the skills necessary to navigate, succeed, and contribute in a rapidly changing world. We are a public comprehensive university, with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary, deeply committed to excellence and free inquiry in research, teaching and learning, and to supporting the aspirations of regional communities while having a global impact. We forge and strengthen meaningful connections within and between our communities, both on and off campus, and with our alumni community. Together we transform lives and communities. In 2025, ULethbridge launched its new strategic plan, a shared vision to challenge boundaries and inspire curiosity; be a place where people aspire to learn, work, and contribute; engage communities and shape the future. To learn more, please visit: https://www.ulethbridge.ca/strategic-plan The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. About Lethbridge Living and benefiting from the Blackfoot Confederacy’s traditional territory, Iniskim (ULethbridge) acknowledges and deeply appreciates the Siksikaitsitapi peoples’ connection to their traditional territory and honour the traditions of the Blackfoot people who have cared for this land since time immemorial. Home to more than 100,000 people, Lethbridge is a place where ideas grow. It is a culturally vibrant city with a flourishing arts scene and an active social calendar. We boast stunning scenery, four distinct seasons, spectacular sunrises and glowing sunsets that illuminate Alberta’s big sky. The University sits on the beautiful coulees, looking over the Old Man River. Lethbridge is only two hours from Calgary’s International Airport and a short drive to the mountainous Waterton Lakes National Park. Lethbridge is an affordable city, with many beautiful neighborhoods on both sides of the coulees and well-planned parks connected via walking and biking paths. Position Category Faculty Faculty of Arts & Science Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9391": {
      "title": "Faculty of Education - THREE (3) Assistant Teaching Professor (Term), Early Years, Elementary, and/or Middle School",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Education - THREE (3) Assistant Teaching Professor (Term), Early Years, Elementary, and/or Middle School Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Education - THREE (3) Assistant Teaching Professor (Term), Early Years, Elementary, and/or Middle School Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications must be submitted online, and should include: a letter of application (2 page max.) outlining their experience with and knowledge with specific attention to the above-described needs; a detailed academic curriculum vitae including the names and contact information for three referees; a teaching philosophy statement (1 page max.) that clearly articulates the applicant’s commitment to accessibility, belonging and community; and a two page proposed outline for a course for a proposed interdisciplinary Curriculum and Instruction course in Humanities, STEM and/or Creative Arts for the Bachelor of Education Early Years program. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Education - THREE (3) Assistant Teaching Professor (Term), Early Years, Elementary, and/or Middle School About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Assistant Teaching Professor Tenure Information Term Position Details Position Details As a result of receiving Targeted Enrolment Expansion funding from the Government of Alberta, the Faculty of Education is pleased to be seeking THREE (3) dynamic and innovative educators whose academic work and experience demonstrates in depth knowledge and understanding of the relationship between theoretical knowledge and professional practice to provide high-quality preparation of future teachers. Successful applicants should be experienced educators and collaborative colleagues for one of THREE (3) full time, two-year term Assistant Teaching Professor positions in the area(s) of early years, elementary, and/or middle school education . Academic duties include (a) teaching assigned courses during the Fall, Winter, and/or Summer sessions, including the organization, preparation, and delivery of course material, the evaluation of students’ academic progress, and, individual discussions with students outside of class; (b) other forms of teaching including but not limited to: tutorial teaching and practicum supervision; © administrative and committee work at various levels – Faculty, University and Association – including academic administration, assistance at registration, and supervision. Of note, our Faculty of Education has a deep commitment to educating its students for a Southern Alberta context. Qualifications, Knowledge & Skills An Assistant Teaching Professor shall possess a graduate degree in a relevant field of study at the time of appointment; a completed or nearly completed doctoral degree would be considered an asset. An equivalent professional designation, or a lesser academic qualification plus appropriate experience may also be considered. Qualifications and/or experience should be directly relevant to early years, elementary, and/or middle school education. Applicants should have 6-10 years of school-based teaching experience in early years, elementary, and/or middle school education, preferably in the Province of Alberta. Candidates should ideally possess teacher certification in Alberta or be eligible for Alberta certification. The successful candidates should have the ability and interest to teach courses in and contribute to the growth of four-year Bachelor of Education Early Years degree and bring expertise in integrating subject areas, with strength in Humanities, STEM and/or Creative Arts. The ability to teach in a primarily face-to-face modality is essential. The ability to integrate innovative technology into teaching will be assets for this position. As a destination university, prospective applicants are expected to reside in or near, and if necessary, relocate to, Lethbridge, Alberta to support students in person and actively engage in our university culture. Fluency in English is a requirement. Proficiency in a second language is an asset. In addition to scholarly expertise, experience, and/or ability to teach in subject areas directly related to early years, elementary, and/or middle school education, the ability to contribute scholarly expertise or experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: Interdisciplinary teaching and learning, particular to Humanities, STEM or Creative Arts. Teaching and learning in complex classroom spaces. Student success in inclusive learning environments. Diverse cultural and linguistic knowledges Sociological, philosophical, historical and cultural influences and issues affecting learning and teaching in school environments. Approaches to addressing accessibility, belonging, community and decoloniality. The University of Lethbridge is committed to creating an inclusive, diverse, and representative workforce that is reflective of the community we serve. The University welcomes all applications from qualified candidates including all employment equity groups of Indigenous people, women, persons with disabilities, racialized individuals and persons of diverse gender and sexual orientation protected under the Alberta Human rights code. In accordance with the Canadian Immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. About our Faculty Situated in the heart of Blackfoot territory on its lands and waters, the University of Lethbridge (Iniskim)’s Faculty of Education (Iinooikaksini) seeks to respectfully honour and work alongside in supporting the advancement of Blackfoot culture, language, and values. Built on an ethic of care, we are committed to act upon principles of fairness, equity, belonging and decoloniality in all our relations. By respectfully modelling diverse approaches to research, teaching and service, we continually strive to enable undergraduate and graduate students to become caring, creative, and critical teachers, counselors, researchers, and leaders. Through innovative, thoughtful, and accessible practices informed by our expertise, we prepare professionals to effectively engage with educational complexities both known and yet to be revealed. Central to these commitments is endeavouring to be local, national, and international leaders in education, counselling, and research. About our programs The Faculty of Education offers three pathways to a highly regarded undergraduate-level bachelor’s degree leading to teacher certification. Information about our undergraduate programming can be found at https://www.ulethbridge.ca/education/undergrad . Our graduate programs in contemporary issues in education and educational leadership offer options for thesis, project and course based. We also offer a Master of Counselling degree and Master of Education in Clinical and Counselling Psychology degree. Details about the Faculty of Education’s graduate programs can be found at https://www.ulethbridge.ca/education/grad . About the University of Lethbridge The University of Lethbridge was established in 1967 with a student population of 638. It has grown to a current population of nearly 9,000 full-time and part-time students, with approximately 766 graduate students and 600 international students from more than 90 countries. Two campuses (Calgary and Lethbridge) and 18 research centres and institutes make up our university community. There are more than 55,000 University of Lethbridge alumni worldwide. The University’s main campus is situated on over 550 acres of traditional Blackfoot territory in west Lethbridge. In the 2024 Maclean’s University Rankings, the University of Lethbridge’s student scholarship support combined with continued excellence in research saw us jump five spots in the primarily undergraduate classification across Canada and number one in Alberta. Student scholarship support saw us leap from 16th to 7th overall in the category. As a testament to the close relationship we have with community partners, our reputation ranking is a solid fourth overall. About the community of Lethbridge The City of Lethbridge is known for being Where the Rocky Mountains meet the Prairies. A city since 1906, Lethbridge is a growing community of just over 100,000 residents, that features affordability and vibrant community engagement. Located in southern Alberta, Lethbridge approximately 145 kilometers east of the Canadian Rockies and 95 kilometers north of the United States border. The city’s economy has expanded from primarily agriculture into a thriving industrial, commercial, research and technology hub. Lethbridge’s major employers are in the education, health care and government sectors. Lethbridge is known for its bright sunshine (more than 320 days per year), warm summers, and mild winters thanks to our semi-arid climate and Chinook winds. The Oldman River divides the north and south sides from the west side. The river valley’s coulees are home to one of North America’s largest urban park systems. With over 240km of trails, enjoy walks, runs and bike rides throughout the city. Adventure is only a short drive away! Experience hiking, camping, skiing and more just outside Lethbridge. Information about Lethbridge can be found at https://www.ulethbridge.ca/about/about-lethbridge Position Category Faculty Faculty of Education Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 01/01/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) 06/30/2029 Special Instructions to Applicants All applications must be submitted online, and should include: a letter of application (2 page max.) outlining their experience with and knowledge with specific attention to the above-described needs; a detailed academic curriculum vitae including the names and contact information for three referees; a teaching philosophy statement (1 page max.) that clearly articulates the applicant’s commitment to accessibility, belonging and community; and a two page proposed outline for a course for a proposed interdisciplinary Curriculum and Instruction course in Humanities, STEM and/or Creative Arts for the Bachelor of Education Early Years program. Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application Statement of Teaching Philosophy Names & Contact Information for 3 Outstanding Academic Referees (Please Condense into 1 Document for Uploading) Sample Course Syllabus Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9370": {
      "title": "Faculty of Arts & Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Faculty of Arts &amp; Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Faculty of Arts & Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Faculty of Arts & Science - Assistant Professor (Psychology) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track Position Details The Department of Psychology invites applications for a Tenure-Track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin 1st July 2027, subject to budgetary approval. Hiring salary will be in the range of $89,064 and $102,100 per year, with starting salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. We are seeking a colleague whose teaching and research focus on any aspect of human cognition, social psychology, or individual differences. Outstanding candidates should also be able to teach a range of junior- and senior-level undergraduate courses in their area of expertise. They will establish and sustain an independent, externally funded research program, demonstrate excellence in engaging and inspiring undergraduate and graduate students, and contribute actively to departmental programs and curriculum development. It is imperative that the successful applicant holds a Ph.D. and at least one graduate degree in Psychology. Our Team: The Department of Psychology has an enthusiastic group of faculty members with diverse and active research programs. Our interests range across various areas of experimental, social and forensic psychology, to sociocultural behaviour in humans and other animals, and aspects of animal communication. The department has an established graduate program and a thriving undergraduate student culture, encouraged through faculty involvement. Our University: The University of Lethbridge (uLethbridge) is a comprehensive and research-intensive university founded on the principles of liberal education where inspired scholars integrate research and creative activity with teaching. Our University’s Blackfoot name is Iniskim, meaning Sacred Buffalo Stone. Founded in 1967 on traditional Blackfoot land, it is a place where student engagement in learning, creative activities, and research takes place every day. With campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary, uLethbridge offers more than 150 undergraduate and 60 graduate programs in the Faculties of Arts & Science, Education, Fine Arts, Health Sciences, the Schools of Liberal Education and Graduate Studies, and the Dhillon School of Business. Together, these programs serve more than 8,500 students. Our Values: The university recognizes that diversity enriches our campus and our community and is fundamental to excellence in teaching, learning, and research. The university as a whole embraces equity as a core value to be truly inclusive of the communities of which we are a part, and this requires ongoing intentional and systemic action. Through recruitment and support of individuals who further enhance our diversity, the University strives to create a diverse and inclusive community where students, faculty and staff feel welcome, are treated equitably, and can thrive. Our City: Living and benefiting from Blackfoot Confederacy’s traditional territory, Iniskim (uLethbridge) is direct neighbours with Kainai Nation , the largest reserve in Canada. We acknowledge and deeply appreciate the Siksikaitsitapi peoples’ connection to their traditional territory and honour the traditions of people who have cared for this land since time immemorial. Home to more than 100,000 people, Lethbridge is a place where ideas grow. It is a culturally vibrant city with a flourishing arts scene and an active social calendar. We boast stunning scenery, four distinct seasons, spectacular sunrises and glowing sunsets that illuminate Alberta’s big sky. The University sits on the beautiful coulees, looking down on the Old Man River. Lethbridge is only two hours from Calgary’s International Airport and a short drive to the mountainous Waterton Lakes National Park. Looking for a centre with a lower cost of living than many other Canadian cities? See the Canadian Real Estate Association national price map to compare average Canadian housing prices. Lethbridge is an affordable city, with many beautiful neighborhoods on both sides of the coulees and well-planned parks connected via walking and biking paths Our Application Process: All applications must be submitted online, and include a letter of application, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching interests and philosophy, outlines of courses previously taught, a statement of research program, teaching evaluations (if available), and the contact information for three references (references will be contacted directly for short-listed candidates). The initial deadline for applications is 28 September 2026 , but the position will remain open until the short-list of candidates is finalized. For enquiries about the position, please contact Dr. Jean-Baptiste Leca, Chair, Department of Psychology, jeanbaptiste.leca@uleth.ca Position Category Faculty Faculty of Arts & Science Campus Lethbridge Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 07/01/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University acknowledges the potential impact that career interruptions can have on a candidate’s record of achievement. We encourage applicants to explain in their application the impact that career interruptions have had on their record. The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Outlines References Letter of Application Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Teaching/Research Interests Statement of Research Program Optional Documents Additional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). I authorize the University of Lethbridge to disclose the personal information submitted as my application package to the search committee and members of the department for the purpose of administering the selection process for this position. This consent is valid for the period of one year from the application date the information is submitted. I agree I don't Agree The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
