    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9380": {
      "title": "Graduate Student Engagement Assistant (Co-op, Full-time, Term)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Graduate Student Engagement Assistant (Co-op, Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Graduate Student Engagement Assistant (Co-op, Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Graduate Student Engagement Assistant (Co-op, Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The School of Graduate Studies ( SGS ) is seeking an enthusiastic and creative undergraduate or graduate co-op student to join our team. This role offers an opportunity to contribute to initiatives that support graduate student success, professional development, well-being, and community engagement. As a member of the SGS team, you will help create meaningful opportunities that connect graduate students with resources, experiences, and information that enhance their graduate journey. This position is ideal for someone who enjoys working on a variety of projects, creating engaging resources, and contributing to a positive and supportive student experience. What You’ll Do Help Graduate Students Thrive Support initiatives that help graduate students succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Contribute to projects that connect students with opportunities, resources, and experiences that enrich their graduate journey. Create Resources That Matter Develop and maintain engaging digital and print resources that help students navigate graduate school and make informed decisions. Assist with website updates, newsletters, social media content, and other materials that keep students connected and informed. Ensure information is clear, accessible, relevant, and student-focused. Foster Connection and Community Help promote programs, services, workshops, and events that encourage student engagement and a sense of belonging. Support efforts that bring graduate students together and strengthen connections across disciplines, research areas, and campus communities. Support Meaningful Projects Collaborate with School of Graduate Studies staff, students, faculty, and campus partners on initiatives that enhance the graduate student experience. Assist with project coordination, resource development, communications, and administrative activities that support program success. Share Ideas and Perspectives Bring creativity, curiosity, and fresh perspectives to student engagement initiatives. Help identify new ways to connect students with opportunities, celebrate successes, and strengthen the graduate community. What You’ll Gain Hands-on experience supporting graduate student success initiatives within a post-secondary environment. Opportunities to develop skills in project coordination, digital content development, engagement, and collaboration. Experience working with diverse campus partners and contributing to initiatives that have a direct impact on students. The opportunity to help shape an inclusive, supportive, and engaging graduate student community at the University of Lethbridge. Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Applicants must be a senior undergraduate or graduate student enrolled in a program eligible for Co-operative Education designation. The successful candidate will demonstrate: Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, including Word, Outlook, Teams, PowerPoint, and Excel. Experience using social media and digital platforms. Familiarity with website content management and digital tools. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities. A genuine interest in student success, community building, and enhancing the graduate student experience. Must be available for in-person work on the Lethbridge Campus. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas: Graphic design and visual content creation (e.g., Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, or similar tools). Photography, photo editing, or multimedia development. Video creation and editing. Website design or content management. Digital engagement and online community building. Accessibility, inclusive design, and user-centred communication practices. Experience working with student groups, community organizations, or post-secondary environments. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $4,390.00 - $4,884.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $4,390.00 - $5,378.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 8) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/13/2026 Close Date 11/08/2026 Open Until Filled No Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/31/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you a current undergraduate or graduate student at the University of Lethbridge? Yes No Will you remain a current student at ULethbridge until the end of the contract on December 31, 2027? Yes No Are you eligible for a Co-Op as part of your academic program? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
