    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9376": {
      "title": "Marketing Production Coordinator (Full-time, Term)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Marketing Production Coordinator (Full-time, Term) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Marketing Production Coordinator (Full-time, Term) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Marketing Production Coordinator (Full-time, Term) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The University of Lethbridge is hiring a Marketing Production Coordinator to support the central Communication, Marketing and Government Relations ( CMGR ) team. In this two-year term position, you’ll play a key part in keeping the university’s marketing efforts moving forward. From coordinating photo and video shoots to tracking timelines, vendors and project logistics, you’ll help connect people, projects and priorities to support recruitment, retention, research and reputation-building initiatives. In this role, you’ll serve as an operational backbone for the Marketing function. You’ll help move projects efficiently from request to execution by gathering requirements, coordinating timelines, organizing details and ensuring creative teams have the information, assets and resources they need to do their work. You’ll keep track of the details that can make or break a project, from confirming shoot logistics and production specifications to following up with vendors and ensuring materials arrive where and when they’re needed. You’ll also support helping serve as a trusted point of contact for campus partners. Success in this role comes from anticipating needs, paying close attention to detail and creating the conditions for great work to happen. We’re looking for a highly organized, service-oriented professional who enjoys improving processes, coordinating complex projects, and ready to jump in with hands on support when needed. Responsibilities include: Coordinate the flow of marketing projects by tracking timelines, tracking deliverables, supporting project intake, and facilitating communication between vendors, stakeholders and marketing team members. Coordinate photography and video projects, including schedules, logistics, locations, documentation and production-related communications. Maintain accurate project documentation, including project briefs, timelines, contact information, approvals, production details, vendor information and project records. Support the production and quality assurance of marketing materials, signage, and promotional items by coordinating with vendors, obtaining quotes, placing orders, and monitoring production/installation schedules. Provide responsive support to internal clients by maintaining shared inboxes, clarifying project needs, coordinating smaller marketing initiatives. Support the administration of the university’s digital signage program. Contribute to departmental operations within a through event support and other marketing and communications initiatives as required. This position reports to the Director of Marketing. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required. We’re a collaborative, creative and student-focused team. If you’re excited to support meaningful marketing initiatives, we want to hear from you. Position Qualifications Diploma in Marketing, Communications, Business Administration, or a related field required; bachelor’s degree preferred. 2-4 years of experience in marketing, communications, project coordination, production coordination, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple projects, timelines, schedules, and competing priorities with a high degree of organization and attention to detail. Experience coordinating photo or video shoots, including talent, locations, releases, call sheets, equipment and day-of production logistics is considered an asset. Working knowledge of print production processes and experience working with external vendors and suppliers. Understanding of marketing and communications principles, including working within established brand standards and guidelines. Strong relationship-building and customer service skills, with the ability to work effectively with external vendors and cross-functional teams. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to gather information, clarify requests, and provide responsive support. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications and collaboration tools, including Microsoft Planner and SharePoint. Experience with digital asset management systems is considered an asset. Ability to work independently while contributing to a fast-paced, deadline-driven team environment. Post-secondary experience is considered an asset. A valid unrestricted Class 5 Driver’s License with no more than 6 demerits and submission of a motor vehicle record (driver abstract) dated within 3 months of the posting close is required. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $4,390.00 - $4,884.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $4,390.00 - $5,378.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 8) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/13/2026 Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 12/01/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/01/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9382": {
      "title": "Industrial Instrumentation Technician (Full-time, Continuing)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Industrial Instrumentation Technician (Full-time, Continuing) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Industrial Instrumentation Technician (Full-time, Continuing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Industrial Instrumentation Technician (Full-time, Continuing) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The University of Lethbridge is seeking a full-time, continuing position as an Industrial Instrumentation Technician. This position is responsible for providing specialized technical expertise, control loop tuning and troubleshooting skills for the development, installation, operation, and maintenance of campus building heating, cooling, humidification, ventilation, and co-generation plant control systems. Additionally, the Instrument Technician calibrates, maintains, and operates safety interlock devices and alarms for campus hot water boilers, steam boilers, chillers, and co-generation equipment to ensure their safe and reliable operation ensuring the protection of students, staff, and university assets. The Instrumentation Technician must have the knowledge and skills required to conduct control system planning, design and mechanical trouble shooting duties, to optimize control system operation, tuning and control components operation. The Instrumentation Technician is responsible for the operation, calibration, and maintenance of numerous life safety equipment systems on campus. This position is expected to assist the Project Management Office with project support when related to HVAC mechanical systems and components, as well as control systems and sequence of operations on the building management systems. This support includes drawing reviews, site inspections, and commissioning duties. This position is a member of a 5-person team who form a weekly rotation for standby duties outside of normal working hours including evenings and weekends. Normal business hours are Monday through Friday, 08:00 – 16:00. Position Qualifications Applicants will have minimum grade 12 education and an Alberta Journeyman Instrumentation & Controls Technician Certificate or out of province Red Seal designation. Preference will be given to those candidates who also possess an Operating Engineer 4th Class certification. Along with the educational background, applicants should have 3 years relevant experience in an industrial or institutional maintenance setting.This experience can be through a combination of apprenticeship and journeyman positions. Certification in any technician level programming certification and greater number of year’s experience are considered assets. Applicants should be able to demonstrate their experience with heating, cooling, humidification, and ventilation equipment. Experience with installing, calibrating, maintaining, and repairing life safety equipment is essential. Additionally, the applicants should possess certificates in the following: WHMIS Personal Fall Protection Mobile Elevating Work Platform H2S Alive Confined Space Entry and Rescue A valid unrestricted Class 5 Driver’s License with no more than 6 demerits and submission of a motor vehicle record (driver abstract) dated within 3 months of the posting close is required. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,782.00 - $6,545.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $5,782.00 - $7,308.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 12) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Other Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/14/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Desired Start Date 11/16/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
