    "https://uleth.peopleadmin.ca/postings/9396": {
      "title": "Executive and Administration Support 6 (Full-time, Continuing)",
      "description": "University of Lethbridge Applicant Portal | Executive and Administration Support 6 (Full-time, Continuing) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Executive and Administration Support 6 (Full-time, Continuing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Executive and Administration Support 6 (Full-time, Continuing) About the University At the University of Lethbridge, we speak in perspectives. We are located in the heart of traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory in southern Alberta with campuses in Lethbridge and Calgary. ULethbridge is more than a place to learn — it’s a place to build a career and make a lasting impact. We are one of Canada’s top universities and leading research institutions with more than 8,000 undergraduate and graduate students. We are an inclusive university that values diverse experiences and backgrounds. Our people are our greatest strength, and we are dedicated to fostering growth and success for all of our people. Together, we transform lives and communities. Position Details The Faculty of Health Sciences at the University of Lethbridge is currently seeking applications for an Executive and Administrative Support position commencing immediately. This is a 1.0 FTE continuing position. The successful candidate will serve as the first point of contact in the Dean’s Office and provide comprehensive administrative support to the Dean’s Office and academic staff. Key duties and responsibilities include front desk reception and responding to general inquiries; word processing and file management; scheduling appointments; managing databases and listservs; coordinating room bookings and supporting special events; providing general program information; liaising with internal and external suppliers and stakeholders, and providing administrative support to various committees. In addition, the position will support faculty communications by managing and updating social media pages, assisting with the creation and distribution of internal and external communications, and developing basic graphic materials (such as posters, digital signage, and social media content) in accordance with Faculty and University branding guidelines. Position Qualifications The ideal candidate will possess a two-year College Diploma in a related field and a minimum of one-year related work experience, an equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Proven administrative skills, as well as an advanced level of proficiency with Microsoft Office (word processing, spreadsheets, presentations, and e-mail and database applications) is essential, as well as familiarity with updating website content. As this is the first point of contact for the Dean’s Office, it is critical that the successful incumbent presents a good first impression. The ideal candidate will be able to build rapport with all members of the University community, have excellent communication skills (oral and written), strong interpersonal and organizational skills, and the ability to work in an environment with numerous competing deadlines. Familiarity with the University of Lethbridge and the ability to work independently within a team structure in a busy office is essential. Other important qualities include professionalism, initiative, patience and flexibility. Starting Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $3,986.00 - $4,410.00 monthly Full Salary Range (at 1.0 FTE) $3,986.00 - $4,833.00 monthly (AUPE - Grade 6) Campus Lethbridge Employment Group AUPE Position Category Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/23/2026 Close Date 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled Desired Start Date 11/09/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Special Instructions to Applicants Employment Equity The University of Lethbridge invites applications from all qualified candidates; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and permanent residents will be given preference. The University of Lethbridge is committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, including through all aspects of the hiring process. If you require support during the hiring process, please contact Human Resources at human.resources@uleth.ca so that accommodations can be put in place to support you. All private information received in relation to your request for support will be kept confidential, only information required to facilitate the accommodation will be shared with the selection committee. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Additional Documents The University is located on traditional Blackfoot Confederacy territory. We honour the Blackfoot people and their traditional ways of knowing in caring for this land, as well as all Indigenous Peoples who have helped shape and continue to strengthen our University community. ©2020 University of Lethbridge | 4401 University Drive, Lethbridge, Alberta T1K 3M4 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
